---
layout: base.njk
title: Professional Record
description: The Professional Record of Albert Chang, an engineer connecting renewable-energy practice with community-centered energy systems and practical infrastructure.
pageModule: /assets/js/experience-timeline.js
---
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">{{ site.brandLine }}</p>
    <h1 id="hero-title">A community-centered engineer translating climate goals into practical infrastructure</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="portrait-placeholder" role="img" aria-label="Portrait placeholder for Albert Chang">
    <span>Portrait placeholder</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="experience" class="section-shell experience-section" aria-label="Experience" data-experience-timeline>
  <h2 id="experience-title">Experience</h2>
  <ol class="experience-timeline" aria-label="Experience Timeline">
    {% for entry in experience %}
      <li class="experience-entry" data-timeline-entry>
        <div class="experience-marker-slot" aria-hidden="true">
          {% if entry.marker %}<img src="{{ entry.marker.src | url }}" alt="">{% else %}<span class="experience-marker"></span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <article>
          <h3>{{ entry.company }}</h3>
          <p class="experience-entry__role">{{ entry.role }}</p>
          <dl class="experience-entry__facts">
            <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>{{ entry.location }}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Dates</dt><dd>{{ entry.startDate }} – {{ entry.currentLabel or entry.endDate }}</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

<section id="about" class="section-shell narrative-section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <h2 id="about-title" class="visually-hidden">About</h2>
  <p>Growing up, my family had air conditioning, but high electricity bills meant rarely using it. Staying comfortable was not only a question of temperature; it was also a decision about cost. That experience gave me an early, personal understanding of energy burden and continues to shape how I think about the infrastructure people rely on.</p>
  <p>Today, I want to help close the gap between how energy systems are modeled and how they are experienced. I am interested in developing renewable-energy projects that are technically grounded and informed by the communities they serve—inviting people to help define problems, making benefits, burdens, and trade-offs visible, and communicating findings in forms people can use. I have been fortunate to learn from supportive institutions and generous mentors. That access shaped my commitment to sharing knowledge, making technical ideas approachable, and giving back as I continue learning and growing.</p>
</section>

<section id="education" class="section-shell education-preview" aria-label="Education Journey preview">
  <h2 id="education-title">Education</h2>
  <p>I earned a B.S. in Mechanical Engineering from UC San Diego and an M.S. in Energy Science, Technology, and Policy from Carnegie Mellon University. Together, those experiences expanded how I understand engineering—from designing physical systems to considering the policies, people, and institutions that shape what gets built. The mentors and learning environments I encountered, along with the free resources I sought out, reinforced my belief that knowledge should be accessible and shared.</p>
  <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/education/' | url }}">Learn More</a>
</section>
